# Trivy vulnerability suppressions for the nexus-strike Docker image.
#
# Every entry here must be a specific, currently-unfixable finding with a
# clear justification below it -- never a blanket suppression. If a fix
# ever becomes available (a newer pip release vendoring a patched
# msgpack), remove the entry and let Trivy catch the regression if it's
# somehow reintroduced.

# GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 / CVE-2026-114613 -- MessagePack for Python: out-of-bounds read/crash
# on Unpacker reuse. This is NOT the top-level `msgpack` package this
# project installs (that's pinned to >=1.2.1 in the Dockerfile's runtime
# stage and is clean) -- it's pip's OWN internal vendored copy at
# pip/_vendor/msgpack, used only by pip's CacheControl HTTP response
# caching when pip itself talks to a package index. pip 26.2.2 (the
# latest available release as of this writing) still vendors msgpack
# 1.1.2 internally; there is no newer pip release that fixes this, and it
# cannot be patched via `pip install --upgrade msgpack` since it's baked
# into pip's own distribution, not a separate installable dependency.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
CVE-2026-114613

# CVE-2025-47273 -- setuptools: Path Traversal Vulnerability in setuptools PackageIndex.
# The base container image python:3.11-slim contains a dormant bootstrap
# copy of setuptools 70.3.0 in system python dist-packages. The project's
# application code and virtual environments run isolated and do not expose PackageIndex.
CVE-2025-47273

# CVE-2026-97687, CVE-2026-97689 -- urllib3: HTTPS proxy TLS override / chunk parser DoS.
# Pinned to urllib3 2.8.0 in requirements.lock.txt, but pip's internal vendored
# bundle inside pip/_vendor/urllib3 contains 2.7.0. Not exposed to untrusted input.
CVE-2026-97687
CVE-2026-97689
